<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Definition of the combined water + meal + expense widget.

  How the size works: a launcher places widgets on a grid of cells, so the size
  is expressed in cells and the launcher translates it to dp.
  - targetCellWidth/targetCellHeight are the size used by launchers on
    Android 12+ (4 columns by 3 rows here: the water card on top, the meal
    card in the middle and the read-only expense card at the bottom — icon
    alone on the left, with the progress component, the numbers and the
    button row grouped in the same box on its right for water and meal, the
    three sections separated by view lines; the meal row swaps between the four
    slot buttons and the Correct / Warning / Wrong chooser, and a completed
    section collapses to a compact line with a check).
  - minWidth/minHeight are the same size in dp, using the formula launchers rely
    on (70dp * cells - 30dp): minWidth = 70*4 - 30 = 250dp,
    minHeight = 70*3 - 30 = 180dp. They are what limits how far the widget can
    be shrunk when resized. The content needs about 240dp of height, so the
    3-row target is the smallest that shows all three sections without clipping.
  - resizeMode allows resizing in both directions. The layout stretches with the
    cell size (the water and meal sections take the leftover height), so there is
    only one layout: onAppWidgetOptionsChanged re-reads the values after a resize.
  - updatePeriodMillis keeps the widget fresh without the app being opened:
    the launcher asks for an update at most every 30 minutes (the smallest
    interval allowed), which is also what moves the widget on to the new day
    after midnight - the water total, the meal segments/count and the expense
    total all roll over.
  - previewLayout makes the picker show the real widget instead of an image.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_combined_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_combined"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="180dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_combined"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
